-- `emit <particle> to core [get <name>]` invokes a compiled-in handler,
-- chosen at runtime by the particle's own "_class" field. What comes back
-- is a particle too, not a bare value — a fresh one, tagged "LengthResult",
-- symmetric with what went in.
emit Length { "value": [1, 2, 3, 4] } to core get n
assert n = { "_class": "LengthResult", "value": 4 }
assert n.value = 4
